// Test fixture: Validator value type with error: usage

Value subclass: Validator

  /// BT-4075: `self` here is a class object, but Validator has no class-side
  /// `error:`, so `self error:` still raises `user_error`.
  class rejectAll => self error: "rejected"

  check: value =>
    value < 0 ifTrue: [self error: "must be non-negative"]
    value

  /// BT-4075: `obj` is untyped, so `obj error:` is decided at run time: a
  /// class object with a class-side `error:` receives the send, anything else
  /// raises.
  raise: msg via: obj => obj error: msg
